<rtept lat="50.8389400000" lon="-0.8963300000">
<time>2026-05-08T14:46:09Z</time>
<name>Water's Edge to Left Turn</name>
<desc>Continue along the path as it arcs around the bottom of the Nutbourne Channel, and if you are walking during the winter months, you will now certainly be in the sight and sound of a number of those 10,000 geese. Keep an eye out to your right into the harbour if the tide is not out, as there are usually seals in Chichester Harbour. You pass an area of trees on the left. At the end of the trees, as the sea wall ends, the harbour edge turns to the right. Take the new path in front of you.</desc>
<sym>Flag</sym>
<type>Marks</type>
